Definition. Let $X$ and $I$ be sets. Then the elements of $\mathrm{Family}$ applied to $X$ and $I$ are a basic type.

By cases: \begin{itemize} \item for $X$ and $I$, the set of elements of $\mathrm{Family}$ applied to $X$ and $I$ is the set of elements of $\F {I}{(\wp X)}$. \end{itemize}

Definition. Let $X$ and $I$ be sets. Let $U$ be a function from elements $i$ of $I$ to elements of $\wp X$. Then $\family {I}{i}{U}$ is an element of $\mathrm{Family}$ applied to $X$ and $I$.

